{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk","lean:module:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.straddling_vertex_coordinates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.straddling_vertex_coordinates","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L139-L144","doc":"Non-vacuity: a γγ vertex straddling the boundary between blocks `0` and `1`\n(position `1`, strands `1, 2, 3`) does coordinate them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.mixedGraph_linearLayout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.mixedGraph_linearLayout","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L129-L137","doc":"**Mixed words.** γγ vertices together with single crossings (the production word's interface\nletters) still give a linear layout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.gammaGammaGraph_linearLayout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.gammaGammaGraph_linearLayout","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L120-L127","doc":"**γγ words.** For any list of γγ vertex positions, the coordination graph on the contiguous\nlayout is a linear layout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.crossingRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.crossingRun","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L117-L118","doc":"A single crossing `σᵢ`, as a run: it touches `{i, i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.ggRun_touches_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.ggRun_touches_iff","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L110-L115","doc":"The run of `ggRun i` is exactly `vertexStrands i`, the support recorded in\n`GammaGammaForcesTheLayout`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.ggRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.ggRun","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L107-L108","doc":"A γγ vertex at position `i`, as a run: it touches `vertexStrands i = {i, i+1, i+2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph_degree_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph_degree_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L101-L105","doc":"Hence every block has at most two coordination neighbours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph_linearLayout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph_linearLayout","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**The bridge.** If every letter touches at most three consecutive strands, the coordination\ngraph on the contiguous layout is a linear layout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.coordGraph","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L78-L88","doc":"The coordination graph of a word on `n` contiguous blocks: distinct blocks `j, k` are\nadjacent when some letter touches a strand of each. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.Touches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.Touches","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L75-L76","doc":"Strand `x` is touched by run `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.width","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.width","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.start","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.start","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.Run","kind":"structure","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L69-L73","doc":"A letter, recorded by the run of strands it touches: start `i`, width `w`\n(it touches `i, …, i + w`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.wide_run_meets_three_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.wide_run_meets_three_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The bound is sharp in the right place: a run of five strands can meet three blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.run_blocks_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.run_blocks_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaLinearLayout.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**The arithmetic core.** Two strands in a run of at most three consecutive strands lie in\nthe same block or in consecutive blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.blockOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaLinearLayout.blockOf","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://